## Usage Examples

### Basic Gameplay
```bash
./tetris                              # Start with default settings
./tetris -l 5                         # Start at level 5
./tetris --map-size=15,8             # Custom board size
./tetris -w                          # Hide next piece preview
```

### Custom Controls
```bash
./tetris -kl 'a' -kr 'd' -kt 'w' -kd 's'    # WASD controls
./tetris --key-pause='p' --key-quit='e'      # Custom pause/quit keys
./tetris -kt ' ' -kp 'p'                     # Space for rotation
```

### Debug and Development
```bash
./tetris -d                          # Debug mode with full diagnostics
./tetris -d --level=3 --map-size=12,6    # Debug with custom settings
```

This implementation provides a complete, production-quality Tetris game with professional-grade architecture, comprehensive customization options, and robust error handling for an authentic classic gaming experience in the terminal environment.